                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "93500ff7-ab02-3aba-9b5b-c01dd3ca8157",
                        "entry_id": "d923f2ab-bdc5-30cf-baf1-3ba5c5770e0e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Turm, von dem aus eine weite Aussicht, Fernsicht möglich ist; meist auf Bergen errichtet"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0c89a90e-4344-4e95-920e-2f3068c5f180",
                                "sense_id": "93500ff7-ab02-3aba-9b5b-c01dd3ca8157",
                                "text": "Von einem Aussichtsturm kann man eine weite Sicht genießen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a6e0f90e-a6c4-4272-b16a-fbc1a4423a18",
                                "sense_id": "93500ff7-ab02-3aba-9b5b-c01dd3ca8157",
                                "text": "„Auf eben dieser Bank, ein Bild des Behagens, saß der alte Stechlin in Joppe und breitkrempigem Filzhut und sah, während er aus seinem Meerschaum allerlei Ringe blies, auf ein Rundell, in dessen Mitte, von Blumen eingefaßt, eine kleine Fontäne plätscherte. Rechts daneben lief ein sogenannter Poetensteig, an dessen Ausgang ein ziemlich hoher, aus allerlei Gebälk zusammengezimmerter Aussichtsturm aufragte.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "13fe9107-cfb5-40e2-bf6a-f1b7dac4caed",
                        "source_entry_id": "d923f2ab-bdc5-30cf-baf1-3ba5c5770e0e",
                        "source_sense_id": "93500ff7-ab02-3aba-9b5b-c01dd3ca8157",
                        "source_sense_description": "Turm für weite Aussicht",
                        "target_lang_word": "watch tower",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "watch tower",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d7ff2d2a-6cf3-304d-b876-0df450341402",
                                        "entry_id": "ba71e877-c682-3838-a9d7-5c9f857f4bcd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of watchtower."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14c758b4-d041-414c-99d4-c035766d1559",
                                                "sense_id": "d7ff2d2a-6cf3-304d-b876-0df450341402",
                                                "text": "For my part, who can now no longer build chateaux even en Eſpagne, I find that Mowbray Caſtle, Graſmere Abbey, the caſtle of Rock-March, the caſtle of Hauteville, and Rayland Hall, have taken ſo many of my materials to conſtruct, that I have hardly a watch tower, a Gothic arch, a cedar parlour, or a long gallery, an illuminated window, or a ruined chapel, left to help myſelf."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2171e55-c5a3-494f-941f-b3c261447b1a",
                                                "sense_id": "d7ff2d2a-6cf3-304d-b876-0df450341402",
                                                "text": "They were interrupted by the entrance of a youth from one of the watch towers of the castle, who communicated intelligence that the army of the Yorkists was in sight."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3db7bbb4-d3a2-44a3-9b3e-d77282db2efb",
                                                "sense_id": "d7ff2d2a-6cf3-304d-b876-0df450341402",
                                                "text": "The walls, moats, gates, and watch towers of the castle remain, but the main keep has not been rebuilt; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6ebb8edf-5e01-489b-906d-ace92d7c7ad1",
                        "source_entry_id": "d923f2ab-bdc5-30cf-baf1-3ba5c5770e0e",
